e6dc1845 (426 1793065403325 "guenchi" (("4gm4c2jr" . 3240) ("w5vbequy" . 14982)) (put ((kind . section) (title . "landing f357") (src . "test: the launcher reads the anchor's group back instead of trusting an errno\n\nlaunch.pl's watcher put the anchor in its own process group and treated\nany failure of that call, and any group it read that was not the\nanchor's, as the anchor having died: no release, the command never ran,\nand the suite log said the anchor died while it was alive, twice on the\nhosted runner (setpgid EPERM), each time a different fixture and green\nalone. An error is not a state. The anchor now sets its own group first\nand reports on the note pipe when it cannot; the watcher reads the\nanchor's group back after its own call, reads once more when the note\npipe turns readable (the anchor writes or closes it only after its own\ncall) within the first deadline, and classifies what it read: the\nanchor's own group, so the release goes on with a note naming the errno;\nanother group, so the run stops as \"group not set\" with the errno, the\ngroup read, the anchor and the watcher's group; ESRCH, the only gone;\nany other read failure, \"group not read\". The test-only --fault-setpgid\ngains two anchor-side modes, anchor-skips and anchor-late, so the rows\nreach the anchor's note and the first wrong-group read whatever the\nscheduling.\n\n- test/launch.pl: the anchor's own setpgid and note; the watcher's read-\n  back, bounded re-read and classification; the fault modes.\n- test/launch-self.sc: ANCHOR-1 rewritten, ANCHOR-4 to ANCHOR-6 new.\n- test/rows-baseline.txt: launch-self 29 rows, 40 lines.\n") (parent . root) (ord . 489))))
