b1cf4d0d (467 1793066541379 "guenchi" (("4gm4c2jr" . 3240) ("w5vbequy" . 14982)) (put ((kind . section) (title . "landing f346") (src . "working views create nothing for a writer that has no draft area\n\nA working view of a writer with no drafts, asked through context, eval,\nexport or the drafts listing, took the writer's draft lock, and taking\nit created the writer's area and its lock file: a read with a misspelt\n--writer left writers/<w>/ behind, while read --working, which takes no\nlock, left nothing. The views now look first, without the lock, for the\nwriter's working/ or structural/ directory: with neither the writer has\nno draft and no structural draft, the answer is the committed one, and\nnothing is created (an area made after that look is a write after the\nread, which the answer never claimed); with either, the lock is taken as\nbefore. Installing and retiring a draft keep the lock and create the\narea on purpose. context.sc's header and the README say so.\n\n- working.sc: with-draft-read before the three read sites.\n- context.sc, README: the sentence.\n- Tests: working-reads-create-nothing (new: every --working consumer\n  leaves no writers/<w>/ for a writer with no drafts); eval-local (the\n  rows that pinned the creation keep their meaning with a pre-made area,\n  and one row reads the new behaviour); rows-baseline.\n") (parent . root) (ord . 491))))
