b2ba4b38 (508 1793248463659 "guenchi" (("4gm4c2jr" . 3240) ("w5vbequy" . 14982)) (put ((kind . section) (title . "landing f367") (src . "import --symbols titles a symbol-cut block the language does not name\n\nA block cut at an editor's symbol by import-code --symbols took its title\nfrom the language's definition patterns only, so a TypeScript class, a\nconst or an export default read \"<lang>:N\" although the symbols file names\nit. The symbols file's name is now kept: a block cut at a symbol carries\nthe symbol's name as its title, but only where the definition patterns\nderive no name for the block's source. Where they derive one, nothing is\nstored and the derived name stays in charge, so a later rename of the\ndefinition is still seen. The first block, which holds the protected\nprefix, takes the last symbol starting at or before the prefix's end. A\nsymbol named \"\" gives no title. Cuts, refusals, split-suggest and plain\nimports are unchanged.\n\n- code-suggest.sc: symbol-line keeps the name; import-symbol-cuts answers\n  the cuts and each block's title.\n- code-project.sc: capture-import adds the title to a titled block.\n- README: the import paragraph says what is stored and that a stored title\n  is the editor's name at the first import, not updated by later edits.\n- Tests: import-symbols (titles, controls for derived names, marked files,\n  plain imports, split-suggest, renames, the first block); rows-baseline.\n") (parent . root) (ord . 498))))
